Copied Types and Constants
Exported to PFS
File Names
This is a quick hack implementation.  Let's do it right someday.

Working Directory
backing: PATH _ NIL;
BackingName: PROC [short: PATH] RETURNS [absolute: PATH] ~ {
SELECT TRUE FROM
backing=NIL => RETURN[NIL];
PFSNames.IsAbsolute[short] => RETURN[NIL];
ENDCASE => absolute _ PFSNames.Cat[backing, short];
absolute _ ResolveRelativeComponents[absolute];
};

SetBacking: PROC [ backingRope: ROPE ] ~ {
backing _ PathFromRope[backingRope];
};
gets the $WorkingDirectory property from the process property list;
if empty, uses the default working directory

File Information

Enumeration
Opening Files
backingName: PATH _ BackingName[name];
[fs, nameOnFS] _ DoServer[backingName];
openFile _ fs.procs.open[fs, nameOnFS, wantedUniqueID, access, checkFileType, fileType, createOptions];
openFile.fullFName _ PFSNames.SetVersionNumber[backingName, openFile.fullFName.ShortName[].version]; 
[] _ FinalizeOps.EnableFinalization[openFile, fq];
